Given :
emp table - empName, empId
sal  table -  empId, amount

Print the output as :
range(0-100000) (100000-200000),   name of employees falling under this category in mysql


emp table:
============
empName	    empId
Alice	      1
Bob           2
Charlie	      3
Dave	      4
Eve	          5


sal table:
===============
empId	 amount
1	      90000
2	     150000
3	     120000
4	     200000
5	      50000

The output of the query will be:
================================

salary_range	employee_names
================================
0-100000	      Alice, Eve
100000-200000	  Bob, Charlie


SQL query:
==========
SELECT
    CASE
        WHEN amount BETWEEN 0 AND 100000 THEN '0-100000'
        WHEN amount BETWEEN 100001 AND 200000 THEN '100000-200000'
        ELSE 'Other'                                     -- You can add more ranges as needed
    END AS salary_range,
    GROUP_CONCAT(empName ORDER BY empName) AS employee_names
FROM
    emp
JOIN
    sal ON emp.empId = sal.empId
GROUP BY
    salary_range
ORDER BY
    FIELD(salary_range, '0-100000', '100000-200000');



